        "ActionParameters": [
          {
            "Id": 2578,
            "GlobalId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
            "ActionId": 561,
            "Name": "Notes",
            "Value": "<p>Monitors the <strong>dbo.DnnSharp_SharpScheduler_FireTriggers</strong> table for excessive numbers of pending database trigger events.</p>\n<p>Each pending event is associated with a specific automation trigger. Under normal conditions, these events are processed quickly and the queue remains small. A growing queue indicates that database trigger events are being generated faster than they can be processed.</p>\n<p>The workflow groups pending events by trigger and generates one alert for each trigger with more than <strong>99</strong> pending events. Alert severity is determined by the number of queued events:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Warning:</strong> 100&ndash;999 pending events</li>\n<li><strong>Medium:</strong> 1,000&ndash;9,999 pending events</li>\n<li><strong>Critical:</strong> 10,000 or more pending events</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The alert includes the trigger identifier, trigger type, pending event count, associated job information, enabled status, and last modified date. If either the job or trigger is disabled, a hint is included indicating that queued events will not be processed until both are enabled.</p>\n<p>This alert helps identify runaway database trigger loops, high-volume database activity, or slow-running automations before the FireTriggers queue grows large enough to affect overall system performance.</p>",
            "ActionStackId": null,
            "ParentParameterId": null,
            "IsExpression": false,
            "OrderIndex": 0,
            "LastModified": "0001-01-01T00:00:00+00:00",
            "LastModifiedBy": null
          }
        ],
        "Parameters": {},
        "Metadata": {},
        "HasActionParameters": false
      },
